@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+# Spec: JSON Merge Patch
+**Standard**: RFC 7396 §2 (algorithm) and §3 (examples). The request cited "RFC 7386"; the JSON Merge Patch
+standard is RFC 7396 (the constitution names it too), so that is what is implemented.
+**API**: `applyMergePatch(target, patch)` exported from `src/index.ts`; returns the merged document.
+## Requirements
+- Patch is an object: target that is not an object is treated as `{}`; each member with value `null` removes that
+  member from the target (absent is fine); other members are merged recursively.
+- Patch is not an object (array, string, number, boolean, `null`): the result is the patch itself. Arrays replace wholesale;
+  a top-level `null` patch yields `null`.
+- Nulls nested in a patch value that replaces a non-object are dropped (the value is merged into `{}`), per the algorithm.
+- Neither argument is modified; the result shares no structure with them (Constitution IV).
+- `__proto__`, `constructor`, `prototype` are ordinary members; prototypes are never affected. Only own members are read.
+- Member order of the target is preserved; new members append.
+- No new error types: every JSON value is a valid patch/target.
+## Assumptions
+- Inputs are JSON values (not undefined/functions). Non-breaking addition; README updated.
